WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.490
Under Yellowstone, USA, magma can sit as
little as 5 kilometres below the surface.

2
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.730
It is not a tall cone, but
a caldera: a huge hollow,

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.670
about 55 by 80 kilometres.

4
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.950
Its largest eruption,
2.1 million years ago,

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.130
produced about 2,450 cubic
kilometres of material.

6
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.070
Mount St Helens, in 1980, produced
about 1 cubic kilometre of ash.

7
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.510
If Yellowstone erupted like that again,
would the other side of the world notice?

8
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.530
Or is it too far away?

9
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.030
In this mission, you'll compare
shield, composite and supervolcanoes.

10
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.490
Then you'll test how far a supereruption's
effects could really reach.

11
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.530
Your mission: decide whether people on
the other side of the world would notice

12
00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.120
a Yellowstone supereruption.
